# mobile/spike/.gitignore — what the spike's toolchain writes, and what the
# owner's own values are (task M0; Check 733).
#
# The install and the build output are reproducible from what IS committed, so
# neither is a source file. `.env` is the third entry and the reason this file
# exists rather than a copy of `mobile/.gitignore`: a local `.env` holds the
# owner's client ids and the two identifiers of a build, and a value in a
# committed file is a value in a public repository. `.env.example` is the file
# that is committed -- it names every variable and no value.

node_modules/
.expo/
.metro-health-check*
dist/
web-build/
*.log

.env
.env.local
